るい人だと いいました。だから みんなが グラントさんを 出しました。グラントさんは「ありがとう」と いいました。「ゆめが かないました」と いいました。", "でも ジョリー・ヘスモンダルさんは マイハラさんを うたがいました。マイハラさんは グラントさんに ウインクしました。ヘスモンダルさんは おこりました。でも それは ちがいました。", "そのあと わるい人たちは ハンナ・フライさんを なかまに しました。フライさんは とても よろこびました。「あなたたちは いい人だと おもいました」と いいました。", "つぎの あさ みんなが あつまりました。だれも いなくなりませんでした。ミランダ・ハートさんは「フライさんは ちがう」と いいました。", "そのあと みんなは 大きな 木で ドアを こわしました。お金や たてを さがしました。マイハラさんと フライさんは たてを みつけました。", "でも マイハラさんは 出ました。マイハラさんは なきました。「みんなと 友だちに なりたかった」と いいました。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["有一个叫《名人叛徒》的电视节目。周四播了新的一集。理查德·E·格兰特参加了。大家都问格兰特。格兰特说自己是坏人。格兰特笑了。", "格兰特在酒吧说自己是坏人。所以大家把格兰特淘汰了。格兰特说“谢谢”。他说“我的梦想实现了”。", "但是朱莉·赫斯蒙达尔怀疑迈哈拉。迈哈拉对格兰特眨了眨眼。赫斯蒙达尔很生气。但那是错的。", "之后坏人把汉娜·弗莱拉进了队伍。弗莱非常高兴。她说“我以为你们是好人”。", "第二天早上大家集合了。没有人消失。米兰达·哈特说“弗莱不一样”。", "之后大家用大木头撞坏了门。他们找钱和盾牌。迈哈拉和弗莱找到了盾牌。", "但是迈哈拉被淘汰了。迈哈拉哭了。她说“我想和大家做朋友”。"], "body": "「セレブリティ・トレイターズ」という テレビ番組が あります。木曜日に 新しい 話が ありました。リチャード・E・グラントさんが 出ました。みんなが グラントさんに ききました。グラントさんは わるい人だと いいました。グラントさんは わらいました。\n\nグラントさんは バーで じぶんは わるい人だと いいました。だから みんなが グラントさんを 出しました。グラントさんは「ありがとう」と いいました。「ゆめが かないました」と いいました。\n\nでも ジョリー・ヘスモンダルさんは マイハラさんを うたがいました。マイハラさんは グラントさんに ウインクしました。ヘスモンダルさんは おこりました。でも それは ちがいました。\n\nそのあと わるい人たちは ハンナ・フライさんを なかまに しました。フライさんは とても よろこびました。「あなたたちは いい人だと おもいました」と いいました。\n\nつぎの あさ みんなが あつまりました。だれも いなくなりませんでした。ミランダ・ハートさんは「フライさんは ちがう」と いいました。\n\nそのあと みんなは 大きな 木で ドアを こわしました。お金や たてを さがしました。マイハラさんと フライさんは たてを みつけました。\n\nでも マイハラさんは 出ました。マイハラさんは なきました。「みんなと 友だちに なりたかった」と いいました。", "body_zh": "有一个叫《名人叛徒》的电视节目。周四播了新的一集。理查德·E·格兰特参加了。大家都问格兰特。格兰特说自己是坏人。格兰特笑了。\n\n格兰特在酒吧说自己是坏人。所以大家把格兰特淘汰了。格兰特说“谢谢”。他说“我的梦想实现了”。\n\n但是朱莉·赫斯蒙达尔怀疑迈哈拉。迈哈拉对格兰特眨了眨眼。赫斯蒙达尔很生气。但那是错的。\n\n之后坏人把汉娜·弗莱拉进了队伍。弗莱非常高兴。她说“我以为你们是好人”。\n\n第二天早上大家集合了。没有人消失。米兰达·哈特说“弗莱不一样”。\n\n之后大家用大木头撞坏了门。他们找钱和盾牌。迈哈拉和弗莱找到了盾牌。\n\n但是迈哈拉被淘汰了。迈哈拉哭了。她说“我想和大家做朋友”。", "text": "「セレブリティ・トレイターズ」という テレビ番組が あります。木曜日に 新しい 話が ありました。リチャード・E・グラントさんが 出ました。みんなが グラントさんに ききました。グラントさんは わるい人だと いいました。グラントさんは わらいました。 グラントさんは バーで じぶんは わるい人だと いいました。だから みんなが グラントさんを 出しました。グラントさんは「ありがとう」と いいました。「ゆめが かないました」と いいました。 でも ジョリー・ヘスモンダルさんは マイハラさんを うたがいました。マイハラさんは グラントさんに ウインクしました。ヘスモンダルさんは おこりました。でも それは ちがいました。 そのあと わるい人たちは ハンナ・フライさんを なかまに しました。フライさんは とても よろこびました。「あなたたちは いい人だと おもいました」と いいました。 つぎの あさ みんなが あつまりました。だれも いなくなりませんでした。ミランダ・ハートさんは「フライさんは ちがう」と いいました。 そのあと みんなは 大きな 木で ドアを こわしました。お金や たてを さがしました。マイハラさんと フライさんは たてを みつけました。 でも マイハラさんは 出ました。マイハラさんは なきました。「みんなと 友だちに なりたかった」と いいました。", "vocab": [{"word": "わるい人", "pos": "noun", "zh": "坏人", "note": "指节目中的叛徒"}, {"word": "出る", "pos": "verb", "zh": "出去、被淘汰", "note": "这里指离开节目"}, {"word": "おこる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "生气", "note": ""}, {"word": "うたがう", "pos": "verb", "zh": "怀疑", "note": ""}, {"word": "なかま", "pos": "noun", "zh": "伙伴、同伴", "note": ""}, {"word": "よろこぶ", "pos": "verb", "zh": "高兴", "note": ""}, {"word": "たて", "pos": "noun", "zh": "盾牌", "note": ""}, {"word": "なく", "pos": "verb", "zh": "哭", "note": ""}], "title_original": "Emotions run high at the round table as Celebrity Traitors banish two players", "summary_original": "Viewers watched to see whether Richard E Grant could save himself at the first round table of the series.", "body_original": "Emotions run high at the round table as Celebrity Traitors banish two players\nBy\nSteven McIntosh\nEntertainment reporter\nPublished\n2 hours ago\nSpoiler warning: This article reveals details from the third episode of The Celebrity Traitors, series two.\nWe normally expect raised voices, conflicting theories and a dramatic showdown from the Celebrity Traitors. But as this year's first round table got under way, the writing was on the castle wall.\nViewers who often get frustrated with the faithful and root for them to uncover a traitor had their wish firmly Richard E Grant-ed on Thursday, as the actor was banished in a landslide vote.\nHis questionable strategy of revealing he was a traitor to the other celebrities in the bar led to the first time in the UK version of the show that a traitor has been identified at the opening round table.\n\"Thank you for giving me an almost bingo full-house of votes,\" Grant told his fellow players. \"I have always wanted to be a traitor, and sometimes in life your dreams do come true.\"\nThere was jubilation from the other celebrities as Grant confirmed his identity, waving his hands in the air. Ross Kemp was so happy it came out as borderline anger, with a vein-popping \"get in there!\"\nOther players seemed genuinely shocked. \"This is me with men all the time,\" joked comedian Joanne McNally, who hadn't voted for Grant. \"I completely believed him!\"\nBut although the faithful had successfully found a traitor, and even managed to spell his name correctly on their slates, the first round table saw some other players behave in ways that immediately aroused suspicion.\nJulie Hesmondhalgh noticed Myha'la ostentatiously winking at Grant before she voted for him, which later prompted the former Coronation Street actress to make one of the most impassioned - but mistaken - speeches of the night.\n\"It was traitor-on-traitor,\" she declared (it wasn't). \"I don't know if anybody else saw it,\" (we did). \"I am so excited because I truly believe we can get two in a row,\" (don't count on it).\nWhere is the Traitors castle, and can you visit it?\nTraitors commit first murder as Grant tries to save his skin\nCelebrity Traitors cast: Who are this year's 'big dogs' and dark horses?\nThe remaining traitors, Maya Jama and James Acaster, met in the turret later with the choice of murdering previously shortlisted players Jerry Hall and Hannah Fry, or seducing a third traitor to replace Grant.\nThe pair ultimately decided to recruit mathematician Fry, who had the most wonderful and meme-able reaction when she found out that, not only was she not being murdered, she was being seduced.\nAccepting the offer, Fry joined Jama and Acaster in the turret, exclaiming as she learned their identities: \"I had both of you down as faithful!\"\nThe new trio discussed how they would approach breakfast the next morning, before Acaster delivered the line of the episode.\n\"It's changing a lot, this Traitors,\" he observed of the fluid line-up. \"It's like the Sugababes.\"\nThe next morning, there were shocked faces when the players realised everybody had made it to breakfast unscathed, with the celebrities concluding that one player must have been recruited.\n\"It was fascinating seeing Jerry and Hannah come back,\" said Miranda Hart. \"Hannah seemed different, as if something new has happened to her.\" Oh yes? \"I definitely clocked a nervousness in her, which is very interesting.\"\nWe could have a first-rate traitor hunter on our hands here. But would any of Hart's fellow players feel the same way? \"Poor Hannah,\" said McNally, \"she's been recruited.\" Uh-oh.\nAs the theories continued to float around across various sub-meetings, with Hesmondhalgh, Bella Ramsey and several others setting their sights on Myha'la, the celebrities headed out to the next mission.\nPresenter Claudia Winkleman explained the latest task would see them use a battering ram to break down the doors of four crypts, where they could find money to add to the prize pot - and also potentially bag some shields.\nJames Blunt immediately took control, assigning players various roles. \"He was full army officer,\" Hart observed. \"I found it mildly erotic.\"\n\"I don't think I've ever used a battering ram,\" Joe Lycett reflected. \"I would use a battering ram to get into [Wicked star] Jonathan Bailey's house, but that's it.\"\nMyha'la and Fry entered one crypt, found a shield and debated who should keep it. They agreed on Myha'la, partly because she had grabbed it first, although she sweetly suggested that the pair could keep it secret from the other players to protect both of them.\nJama and Sharon Rooney, meanwhile, scored two further shields, but the players then found that some shields would have to be given up anyway in order to unlock the final chest of prize money.\nRooney and Myha'la surrendered theirs, but traitor Jama quietly held on to hers. The other players didn't know she had one, and the TV presenter asked Rooney to keep it secret. That decision could come back to bite her in later episodes.\nIn the cars on the way back, the players continued to debate various hunches, with one particularly awkward journey where Myha'la and Hesmondhalgh admitted they were suspicious of each other.\n\"I feel like you've been a little bit vague,\" said Hesmondhalgh. \"That's only because I've thought it's been you from day one,\" Myha'la replied.\nWe've certainly come a long way from the pair's first exchange just two episodes ago. \"It's lovely to meet you Myha'la, I'm such a big fan!\" - \"Oh my God, thank you!\"\nBack in the castle, Rob Beckett had adopted a new policy. \"When someone comes up to talk to me, I just agree with them, whatever they say,\" he laughed in the castle's diary room.\nAs the players gathered for the second banishment of the episode, discussion inevitably turned to prime suspect Myha'la.\n\"I've heard my name a whole bunch today,\" she acknowledged, as the others struggled to square her behaviour during the mission.\nThe actress became visibly emotional as she recounted the events of the crypt and attempted to justify grabbing the shield before offering it to Fry.\n\"I was going to give it to her,\" Myha'la said tearfully. \"I was worried about my protection, but I thought maybe [Fry] had more heat.\"\nSensing that the tide was turning against Myha'la, Fry stuck the knife in. \"Why would you scrabble for the shield, and then be keen to give it away?\" she asked.\nWatch on iPlayer with new episodes every Thursday and Friday\nThe latest banished and murdered celebs have their say in Uncloaked\nDespite a sprinkling of votes for other players, Myha'la became the second casualty of the episode. \"I have loved getting to know you all,\" she said as she confirmed her faithful status to the other players.\nHart became even more suspicious of Fry, however, after realising the mathematician had orchestrated events to make Myha'la's behaviour at the crypt look less innocent. \"Miss Marple is so on,\" Hart said with a smile.\nLater, the traitors met in the turret and debated who their next victim should be, settling on a shortlist of Blunt, Ramsey and Sebastian Croft.\nAcaster had a characteristically unique reason for suggesting James Blunt.\n\"It would make my life easier,\" he said, \"because every time someone says 'James', I'm turning around, and half the time, it's for him.\"\nCelebrity Traitors continues on Friday at 20:00 BST on BBC One and iPlayer.\nRelated topics\nTelevision\nMore on this story\nCelebrity Traitors: Can I visit the castle, ride the train and see the unusual monument?\nPublished\n1 October\nTraitors claim their first victim as Richard E Grant tries to save his skin\nPublished\n5 days ago\nCelebrity Traitors 2 cast: Who are this year's 'big dogs' and dark horses?\nPublished\n27 September\nChaos, coffins and 'Claudiapatra' steal the show in Celebrity Traitors\nPublished\n6 days ago\nThe Celebrity Traitors connections that might surprise you\nPublished\n4 days ago", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T01:25:53.633209", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "「", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.02, "sm": 0, "em": 20, "cs": 0, "ce": 1, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "セレブリティ", "s": 0.125, "e": 1.025, "sm": 125, "em": 1025, "cs": 1, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "・", "s": 1.025, "e": 1.2, "sm": 1025, "em": 1200, "cs": 7, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "トレイターズ", "s": 1.2, "e": 1.913, "sm": 1200, "em": 1912, "cs": 8, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "」", "s": 1.913, "e": 2.05, "sm": 1912, "em": 2050, "cs": 14, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "と", "s": 2.05, "e": 2.15, "sm": 2050, "em": 2150, "cs": 15, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "いう", "s": 2.163, "e": 2.45, "sm": 2162, "em": 2450, "cs": 16, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "テレビ", "s": 2.462, "e": 2.825, "sm": 2462, "em": 2824, "cs": 19, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "番組", "s": 2.837, "e": 3.288, "sm": 2837, "em": 3287, "cs": 22, "ce": 24, "si":